    <item>
      <title>PROMIS: A Post-Processing Framework for Mitigating Spatial Bias</title>
      <link>https://dsachar.net/publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://dsachar.net/publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In many cases, it is important to ensure that a model does not discriminate against individuals on the basis of their &lt;em&gt;location&lt;/em&gt; (place of origin, home address, etc.). We consider location as the &lt;em&gt;protected attribute&lt;/em&gt; and we want the algorithm to exhibit &lt;em&gt;spatial fairness&lt;/em&gt;
For example, consider a model that predicts whether mortgage loan applications are accepted. Its decisions should not discriminate based on the home address of the applicant. This could be to avoid redlining, i.e., indirectly discriminating based on ethnicity/race due to strong correlations between the home address and certain ethnic/racial groups, or to avoid gentrification, e.g., when applications in a poor urban area are systematically rejected to attract wealthier people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;















&lt;figure  id=&#34;figure-discovered-areas-in-the-usa-where-spatial-unfairness-exists-for-mortgage-loan-applications&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;image&#34; srcset=&#34;
               /publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/spatial_hu8240665862697724322.webp 400w,
               /publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/spatial_hu4086708590153223242.webp 760w,
               /publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/spatial_hu8185717874908182342.webp 1200w&#34;
               src=&#34;https://dsachar.net/publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/spatial_hu8240665862697724322.webp&#34;
               width=&#34;760&#34;
               height=&#34;374&#34;
               loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;
      &lt;em&gt;Discovered areas in the USA where spatial unfairness exists for mortgage loan applications.&lt;/em&gt;
    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This work introduces PROMIS, a post-processing optimization framework designed to reduce spatial bias while maintaining predictive performance. Building on threshold-based equal opportunity adjustments and a robust definition of spatial fairness, PROMIS formulates an optimization problem that minimizes a normalized Spatial Bias Index (SBI), which quantifies expected spatial bias across regions. Unlike heuristic correction methods, PROMIS derives globally optimal, interpretable, and computationally efficient fairness adjustments through mathematical optimization, and, unlike white-box approaches, it can be applied to any classification model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;















&lt;figure  id=&#34;figure-overview-of-the-promis-framework-for-spatial-bias-mitigation-regions-are-colored-by-bias-based-on-true-positive-rates-tprs-blue-unfavored-red-favored-and-grey-fair-left-a-global-threshold-05-produces-tpr-disparities-across-regions-right-promis-applies-region-specific-thresholds-aligning-tprs-and-reducing-spatial-bias-as-reflected-by-the-shift-to-grey-in-the-bar-plots&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;image&#34; srcset=&#34;
               /publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/PROMIS_hu5893642958215238676.webp 400w,
               /publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/PROMIS_hu214848055143811853.webp 760w,
               /publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/PROMIS_hu10781782014680487505.webp 1200w&#34;
               src=&#34;https://dsachar.net/publication/2025-sigspatial-ksg/PROMIS_hu5893642958215238676.webp&#34;
               width=&#34;760&#34;
               height=&#34;138&#34;
               loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;
      &lt;em&gt;Overview of the PROMIS framework for spatial bias mitigation. Regions are colored by bias based on true positive rates (TPRs): blue (unfavored), red (favored), and grey (fair). Left: a global threshold (0.5) produces TPR disparities across regions. Right: PROMIS applies region-specific thresholds, aligning TPRs and reducing spatial bias, as reflected by the shift to grey in the bar plots.&lt;/em&gt;
    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>HYPPO - Using Equivalences to Optimize Pipelines in Exploratory Machine Learning</title>
      <link>https://dsachar.net/publication/2024-icde-kss/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 13 May 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://dsachar.net/publication/2024-icde-kss/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We propose HYPPO, a novel system to optimize pipelines encountered in exploratory machine learning. HYPPO exploits alternative computational paths of artifacts from past executions to derive better execution plans while reusing materialized artifacts. Adding alternative computations introduces new challenges for exploratory machine learning regarding workload representation, system architecture, and optimal execution plan generation. To this end, we present a novel workload representation based on directed hypergraphs, and we formulate the problem of discovering the optimal execution plan as a search problem over directed hypergraphs and that of selecting artifacts to materialize as an optimization problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;















&lt;figure  id=&#34;figure-overview-of-the-pipeline-optimization-process-in-hyppo&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;image&#34; srcset=&#34;
               /publication/2024-icde-kss/hyppo_hu404116620875622785.webp 400w,
               /publication/2024-icde-kss/hyppo_hu15888269972784408355.webp 760w,
               /publication/2024-icde-kss/hyppo_hu16943492095135828721.webp 1200w&#34;
               src=&#34;https://dsachar.net/publication/2024-icde-kss/hyppo_hu404116620875622785.webp&#34;
               width=&#34;760&#34;
               height=&#34;548&#34;
               loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;
      &lt;em&gt;Overview of the pipeline optimization process in HYPPO.&lt;/em&gt;
    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
